#	This file is a sample RADIUS dictionary for MERIT RADIUS server to
#	interact with 3Com Hiper Access Router Card, which is a part of 3Com 
#	Total Control Chassis Product.
#
#	This file contains dictionary translations for parsing
#	requests and generating responses.  All transactions are
#	composed of Attribute Value Pairs.  The value of each attribute
#	is specified as one of four data types.  Valid data types are:
#
#
#       The following conventions must be followed:
#
#       1. The attribute name must be unique
#       2. The client description name must be unique
#
#       The value of each attribute is specified as one of the following
#               data types:
#
#       1. string - string data, 0-253 octets
#       2. data - binary data, 0-253 octets
#       3. ipaddr - 4 octets in network byte order
#       4. integer - 32 bit value in big endian order (high byte first)
#       5. short - 16 bit value in big endian order (high byte first)
#       6. octet - 8 bit value
#       7. tag-int - single octet followed by three octets of integer value
#       8. tag-string - single octet followed by 0-252 octets
#       9. vendor - octet #0 is zero, then three octets IANA #, then vendor defined
#       10. date - 32 bit value in big endian order - seconds since
#                               00:00:00 GMT,  Jan.  1,  1970
#
#	Enumerated values are stored in the users file with dictionary
#	VALUE translations for easy administration.
#	
#	For convenience the standard attributes are denoted in decimal numbers 
#	and the Vendor Specific Attributes are mentioned in hex format.
#
#	Integer values listed below with the same dictionary VALUE "name"
#	MUST be assigned the same numerical value.
#
#	Example:
#
#	ATTRIBUTE	  VALUE
#	---------------   -----
#	Framed-Protocol = PPP
#	7		= 1	(integer encoding)
#

#
#++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
# STANDARD RADIUS ATTRIBUTE SECTION
#++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
#

